  "scoreContext": "Comparative warm-cartoon quality at the registered use size, retaining the same approved-body scores. This followup does not reopen body modeling or claim a 2D food insert is a modeled3D dish. Exact canonical image/aspect/support and visible no-regression are the principal new outcomes.",
  "observations": [
    {
      "criterion": "food-readable-canonical",
      "finding": "The orange salmon bands, white rice and warm ivory plate read cleanly at logical size in S/E and the visible W portion. The round02 plate is slightly warmer than the old gray-white insert, with the approved canonical design intact. It does not look stretched or enlarged; the same occupied width is retained while padded original quad dimensions are corrected."
    },
    {
      "criterion": "real-support-and-occlusion",
      "finding": "Across all96 active hold/load frames, the plate lower contour retains the source support presentation and continuous motion relative to the hands. The E/W/S contact extrema and enlarged palm/plate/face contexts show no new hovering gap or detached plate travel. The same nonzero original billboard world-depth relation is preserved; this is a visual support comparison, not a literal3D zero-gap claim."
    },
    {
      "criterion": "rear-crescent-and-profiles",
      "finding": "Every24 N hold/load frame was inspected against source on light/gray/dark enlarged rear-crescent sheets as well as the full logical sheets. The tiny pale crescent below the rear hair/head remains a thin, intermittent baseline sliver. Canonical ivory makes it quieter in several frames; no materially enlarged bar, head patch or temporal flash appears. Load middle frames conceal it as before. E/W plate and head occlusion remains coherent with the source; eyes stay legible in the required profile context."
    },
    {
      "criterion": "body-face-light-no-regression",
      "finding": "Ama keeps dark-brown skin, short dark fringe, yellow folded wrap, ivory coat, green apron AND necktie, dark shoes and the approved soft highlights. Native old/new face/body comparisons and independent fresh candidate renders show no material skin-color, expression, shadow or volume regression. Actual changed-food radiance residuals are larger than replay variation and are accepted by their observed mild visual effect, not dismissed as noise."
    },
    {
      "criterion": "temporal-and-deadspots",
      "finding": "All192 native frames on three backgrounds retain the approved silhouette and stable foot/hand/knife motion. Hold plate scale/support stays steady; the load rise and return remain continuous without swimming, alpha popping, food tunneling, new black/bright patches, clipped salmon, objectionable halos or a new lighting dead spot. Actual12fps playback and ordered decoding preserve source timing; load is nonloop and ends at11, while idle/work/hold loop."
    },
    {
      "criterion": "scope-and-visual-improvement",
      "finding": "Round02 completes the canonical catalog-food followup while retaining the visibly improved approved warm native body. Useful body modeling from round01 remains intact; original unrefined proportions/part counts and the target lighter skin or framing artifacts were not reinstated as constraints."
    }
  ],
